  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the plane region bounded by the curves $x+2 y^2=0$ and $x+3 y^2=1$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vm2nW",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{5}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "i6R9j",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "A8eFZ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qGiEF",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{4}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Solving the equations we get the points of intersection $(-2,1)$ and $(-2,-1)$\nThe bounded region is shown as shaded region.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { The required area }=2 \\int_0^1\\left(1-3 y^2\\right)-\\left(-2 y^2\\right) \\\\\n& =2 \\int_0^1\\left(1-y^2\\right) d y=2\\left[y-\\frac{y^3}{3}\\right]_0^1=2 \\times \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{4}{3} .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6ks_u_C7uIfyc-XwmaLvr7-H92Y9SsLT-6bf_vVoZyk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
